Adapted code

The Realtek USB Ethernet driver -- named by what it is as well as by
where it lives, kernel/drivers/net/rtl_usb.c with rtl8153.c and
rtl8156.c beside it, because the file has moved once already -- is
original work under the MIT License above, written against FreeBSD's
ure(4) driver (sys/dev/usb/net/if_ure.c and if_urereg.h) as its
reference; the RTL8156/8156B sequence was adapted from the same file on
2026-09-09.

Register addresses, bit definitions and descriptor layouts are facts
about the Realtek hardware and carry no notice. What this notice covers
is the ORDER of the initialisation sequence and the reasoning about
which register writes that sequence needs, both of which were taken from
ure(4). Linux's r8152.c describes the same hardware and is GPL-2.0; it
was deliberately not consulted, because this repository is MIT.

The RTL8111/8168 PCI Express Ethernet driver,
kernel/drivers/net/r8169.c, is original work under the MIT License
above, written against FreeBSD's re(4) driver (sys/dev/re/if_re.c and
sys/dev/rl/if_rlreg.h) as its reference. The same split applies: the
register map and descriptor layout are facts about the hardware, and
what the reference supplied is the ORDER of the bring-up -- in
particular that the receive configuration is written AFTER the receive
engine is enabled. Linux's r8169.c describes the same hardware and is
GPL-2.0; it was deliberately not consulted, for the same reason.

  Copyright (c) 1997, 1998-2003 Bill Paul <wpaul@windriver.com>
  All rights reserved.

Both are under BSD-2-Clause, which is compatible with the MIT License
and requires only that the notice travel with the source:

  Copyright (c) 2015-2016 Kevin Lo <kevlo@FreeBSD.org>
  All rights reserved.

  Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
  modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions
  are met:
  1. Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright
     notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer.
  2. Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright
     notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer in
     the documentation and/or other materials provided with the
     distribution.

  THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY THE AUTHOR AND CONTRIBUTORS ``AS IS''
  AND ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED
  TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A
  PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE DISCLAIMED.  IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR OR
  CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL,
  SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT
  LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF
  USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND
  ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY,
  OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT
  OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF
  SUCH DAMAGE.

