Third-party data

userland/lib/usnd_mp3_tables.h holds three tables defined by ISO/IEC
11172-3 for MPEG-1 Audio Layer III: the Huffman codeword tables, the
512-tap polyphase synthesis window, and the scalefactor band edges.
None of them has a generating formula, so they were taken rather than
written. tools/gen_mp3_tables.py is how they were recovered, and re-running it
reproduces the header byte for byte: it walks both sources back to the
standard's own form and refuses to write anything unless they agree
entry for entry. They were recovered from two public-domain
implementations --
minimp3 (https://github.com/lieff/minimp3, CC0 1.0 Universal) and PDMP3
(https://github.com/technosaurus/PDMP3, the Unlicense) -- and
cross-checked against each other: all fifteen Huffman tables agree
entry for entry between the two, and each is independently verified to
be a complete prefix code.

NOTHING IS LEGALLY OWED FOR THIS. CC0 and the Unlicense are public
domain dedications: no attribution, no notice, no share-alike, and the
result is simply MIT like the rest of this repository. It is recorded
here anyway, because the point of this file is that a reader can learn
where material in the tree came from -- which is the same reason
tools/check_licenses.py exists. The decoder itself
(userland/lib/usnd_mp3.c) is original work under the MIT License above;
what was taken is the standard's data, not anyone's code.

data/pci.ids (seeded onto the disk image as
/usr/share/hwdata/pci.ids, and read by /bin/lspci) is a verbatim copy
of the PCI ID Database maintained by the PCI ID Project at
https://pci-ids.ucw.cz/. It is not covered by the MIT License above.

data/usb.ids (seeded as /usr/share/hwdata/usb.ids,
and read by /bin/lsusb) is a verbatim copy of the USB ID Database
maintained by Stephen J. Gowdy at https://www.linux-usb.org/usb-ids.html.
It is likewise not covered by the MIT License above.

Upstream offers BOTH files under either the GNU General Public License
version 2 or later, or the 3-clause BSD License. toy-os redistributes
them under the 3-clause BSD option, reproduced in full below. Each
file's own header comments -- which name the maintainers -- are
preserved verbatim in the copies shipped here. (usb.ids carries no
licence grant in its own header; the grant is the one published on the
project's page above, and matches the one hwdata ships it under.)

Copyright (c) The PCI ID Project contributors.
Copyright is held by Martin Mares and Albert Pool, and covers the
aggregation and formatting of the data only, the data itself being
factual.

Copyright (c) Stephen J. Gowdy and the USB ID Database contributors,
on the same terms and for the same reason.

Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are
