data/usr/share/terminal/ holds the GUI Terminal's colour schemes. Three
carry another project's palette -- sixteen colour values each, and no
code:

  solarized-dark.scheme     Solarized, Copyright (c) 2011 Ethan
  solarized-light.scheme    Schoonover, under the MIT License
                            (https://github.com/altercation/solarized),
                            whose permission notice is the one at the
                            top of this file. The copyright line is
                            also in each file's header.
  tango.scheme              The Tango Desktop Project's palette,
                            released into the public domain.
  slate.scheme              The colour values of KDE Konsole's
                            Breeze.colorscheme. That file carries no
                            licence header of its own; Konsole as a
                            whole is GPL-2.0-or-later.

amber.scheme, default.scheme and green.scheme are original.

/etc/kbs/* on a built disk image (keyboard layouts, read by
kernel/lib/keyboard_layout.c) is NOT in this repository: tools/gen_kbs.py
generates it at build time from the BUILD HOST's own xkeyboard-config
data, through xkbcli, when that tool is installed. xkeyboard-config is
under X11/MIT-style permissive licences, one per contributor, collected
in its COPYING. What the generated files hold is a key-to-character
table per layout -- no XKB source text -- and a build without xkbcli
ships none, falling back to a compiled-in US table that is original.
An image that carries the layouts also carries those notices, as
/usr/share/licenses/xkeyboard-config.txt: a verbatim copy of
xkeyboard-config 2.48's COPYING, tracked at
data/licenses/xkeyboard-config.txt and seeded by the same Makefile step
that generates the layouts.

---

Everything else

The MIT License at the top of this file governs the rest of this
repository -- all original toy-os source code, documentation and
tooling.

tools/check_licenses.py checks that this inventory stays true: every
vendored port and every shipped font must carry a license file and be
named above. A list kept accurate by somebody remembering is the shape
of every maintenance burden this project has deleted.
